What is the number of bijections $f: \{1, 2, \dots, 9\} \to \{1, 2, \dots, 9\}$ such that, for all distinct $i, j \in \{1, \dots, 9\}$, whenever the squares labelled $i$ and $j$ in the diagram below share an edge, the squares labelled $f(i)$ and $f(j)$ share an edge too?
  \begin{center}
    \begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}
      \hline
      1 & 2 & 3 \\ \hline
      4 & 5 & 6 \\ \hline
      7 & 8 & 9 \\ \hline
    \end{tabular}
  \end{center}
  \begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]
    \item $8$
    \item $9$
    \item $4$
    \item $24$
  \end{enumerate}
